## **PART 5: SECURITY REQUIREMENTS**

**CRITICAL: Review before submitting**

- [ ] Google `client_secret` NEVER appears in Flutter code
- [ ] Google `client_secret` ONLY in backend .env or secrets manager
- [ ] Session tokens are opaque UUIDs (not JWTs with user data)
- [ ] Session tokens never logged in stdout/file
- [ ] User emails/names never logged in plain text
- [ ] All database queries parameterized (no SQL injection)
- [ ] CSRF state token validated on /auth/callback
- [ ] Google ID token signature validated before trusting claims
- [ ] Session expiry enforced: 401 if expired
- [ ] CORS allows only expected origins (not `*`)
- [ ] refresh token endpoint requires valid session (don't create session from nothing)
- [ ] Logout revokes session (is_active = false), doesn't just delete

